module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.CharacterModule
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.DirectSum.GradedSubmodule
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.DirectSum.ParityOperator
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.DifferentialGraded.LeftModule
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.DifferentialGraded.Module.EvaluationAtOne
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-! # The graded `ℚ/ℤ`-dual of a right differential graded module

Let `(A, d)` be a differential graded algebra over a commutative ring `R`. For a *right*
differential graded `A`-module `M`, Stacks 0FQD forms

`M^∨ = Hom^•(M^•, ℚ/ℤ)`,

the graded dual taken into `ℚ/ℤ` placed in degree `0`, and observes that it is a *left*
differential graded `A`-module. This file constructs that module in the bundled encoding of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/DifferentialGraded/LeftModule.lean`, and is the mirror image of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/DifferentialGraded/Module/CharacterDual.lean`, which dualizes a left module
into a right one.

Concretely, `(M^∨)^n` is the group of characters of `M` supported on `M^{-n}`, the left action is
`(a · λ)(x) = λ(x · a)`, and the differential is `λ ↦ (-1)^n (λ ∘ d_M)` on `(M^∨)^n`.

## Main definitions

* `DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual.signedDifferential`: minus the parity operator
  on the degree-`n` part of a right differential graded module.
* `DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual.dualPiece`: the degree-`n` part of the graded dual, as
  a submodule of Mathlib's `CharacterModule`.
* `DifferentialGradedModule.dual`: the graded dual `M^∨`, a left differential graded `A`-module.
* `DifferentialGradedModule.dualRegular`: the graded dual of the regular right module, i.e. `A^∨`
  as a left differential graded `A`-module.

## Main results

* `DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual.dualD0_charSMul`: the Leibniz rule for the dual
  differential.
* `DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual.dualPiece_iSupIndep`: the graded pieces of the dual are
  independent.

## Implementation notes

*`ℚ/ℤ` is Mathlib's `CharacterModule`.* A character of an abelian group `X` is an element of
`CharacterModule X = X →+ AddCircle (1 : ℚ)`, and `AddCircle (1 : ℚ)` is `ℚ/ℤ`. Mathlib already
provides the `R`-module structure, the contravariant action `CharacterModule.dual` on linear
maps, and the exactness and separation lemmas.

*The carrier is a submodule of the full character module, not a direct sum.* The bundled encoding
demands `DirectSum.Decomposition` of the grading, so the carrier of `M^∨` cannot be all of
`CharacterModule M.M` — that is the *product* of the duals of the graded pieces. It is the
submodule `dualSub M` generated by the homogeneous characters, and the decomposition comes from
`Submodule.inducedGrading` together with the independence of the pieces.

*The sign in the differential, and how it differs from the left-module case.* Writing the dual
differential as `λ ↦ ε_n (λ ∘ d_M)` on `(M^∨)^n`, the left-module Leibniz rule
`d (a • λ) = (d a) • λ + (-1)^{deg a} (a • d λ)` forces `ε_n = (-1)^n`, whereas the right-module
Leibniz rule used in `CharacterDual.lean` forces `ε_n = -(-1)^n`. The construction avoids
mentioning `n` by precomposing with `signedDifferential M = -(d_M ∘ DirectSum.parity M.grading)`:
a character of degree `n` is supported on `M^{-n}`, so the only degree at which the sign is seen
is `-n-1`, where the parity operator contributes `(-1)^{-n-1} = -(-1)^n`, and the leading minus
turns this into `(-1)^n`.

*The supporting API lives in the auxiliary namespace `DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual`*,
which keeps the names `dualPiece`, `dualSub`, `signedDifferential` and `dualD0` free in
`DifferentialGradedModule` itself.

*The Leibniz rule needs no support hypothesis.* In the left-module Leibniz rule the sign depends
on the degree of the *algebra* element, which is visible in the statement, so `dualD0_charSMul`
holds for an arbitrary character and the terms involving `d a` cancel identically. Its mirror
image in `CharacterDual.lean` has a sign depending on the degree of the *character*, which is why
that version must hypothesize `l ∈ dualPiece M n` and split into cases.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FQD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FQD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09K3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09K3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

namespace DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {A : DifferentialGradedAlgebra R}

/-- The graded pieces of a differential graded module span it. -/
theorem iSup_grading_eq_top (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : (⨆ n, M.grading n) = ⊤ :=
  ((DirectSum.isInternal_submodule_iff_iSupIndep_and_iSup_eq_top M.grading).mp
    (DirectSum.Decomposition.isInternal M.grading)).2

/-- To prove a property of every element of a differential graded module it suffices to prove it
for homogeneous elements, for `0`, and for sums. -/
theorem induction_homogeneous {M : DifferentialGradedModule A} {p : M.M → Prop} (x : M.M)
    (hmem : ∀ (n : ℤ) (y : M.M), y ∈ M.grading n → p y) (hzero : p 0)
    (hadd : ∀ y z : M.M, p y → p z → p (y + z)) : p x := by
  have hx : x ∈ ⨆ n, M.grading n := by rw [iSup_grading_eq_top]; exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hx using Submodule.iSup_induction' with
  | mem n y hy => exact hmem n y hy
  | zero => exact hzero
  | add y z _ _ ihy ihz => exact hadd y z ihy ihz

/-- The operator `-(d_M ∘ ε)` on a differential graded module, where `ε` is the parity operator
acting as `(-1)^n` on `M^n`. -/
def signedDifferential (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : M.M →ₗ[R] M.M :=
  -(M.d ∘ₗ DirectSum.parity M.grading)

/-- `signedDifferential` acts on a homogeneous element of degree `n` as `-(-1)^n d_M`. -/
theorem signedDifferential_apply_mem (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) {n : ℤ} {x : M.M}
    (hx : x ∈ M.grading n) : signedDifferential M x = -((n.negOnePow : ℤ) • M.d x) := by
  simp [signedDifferential, DirectSum.parity_apply_of_mem M.grading hx]

/-- The signed differential is square-zero, the sign being immaterial to this. -/
theorem signedDifferential_comp_self (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) :
    (signedDifferential M).comp (signedDifferential M) = 0 := by
  ext x
  refine induction_homogeneous (p := fun y => signedDifferential M (signedDifferential M y) = 0)
    x (fun n y hy => ?_) (by simp) (fun y z hy hz => by simp [hy, hz])
  rw [signedDifferential_apply_mem M hy, map_neg, map_zsmul,
    signedDifferential_apply_mem M (M.d_mem n y hy)]
  have := LinearMap.congr_fun M.d_comp_d y
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.zero_apply] at this
  simp [this]

/-! ### The left action on characters -/

/-- The left action of `A` on the characters of a right differential graded module:
`(a · λ)(x) = λ(x · a)`. -/
def charSMul (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (a : A.A) (l : CharacterModule M.M) :
    CharacterModule M.M :=
  l.comp (DistribSMul.toAddMonoidHom M.M (MulOpposite.op a))

/-- The left action `charSMul`, evaluated at a point. -/
@[simp] theorem charSMul_apply (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (a : A.A)
    (l : CharacterModule M.M) (x : M.M) : charSMul M a l x = l (MulOpposite.op a • x) := rfl

/-- `charSMul` makes the characters of a right differential graded `A`-module a left
`A`-module. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def charModule (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : Module A.A (CharacterModule M.M) where
  smul := charSMul M
  one_smul l := by
    ext x
    change l (MulOpposite.op (1 : A.A) • x) = l x
    rw [MulOpposite.op_one, one_smul]
  mul_smul a b l := by
    ext x
    change l (MulOpposite.op (a * b) • x) = l (MulOpposite.op b • (MulOpposite.op a • x))
    rw [MulOpposite.op_mul, mul_smul]
  smul_zero a := by ext x; rfl
  smul_add a l l' := by ext x; rfl
  add_smul a b l := by
    ext x
    change l (MulOpposite.op (a + b) • x) = l (MulOpposite.op a • x) + l (MulOpposite.op b • x)
    rw [MulOpposite.op_add, add_smul, map_add]
  zero_smul l := by
    ext x
    change l (MulOpposite.op (0 : A.A) • x) = 0
    rw [MulOpposite.op_zero, zero_smul, map_zero]

attribute [local instance] charModule

/-- The `A`-action of `charModule`, evaluated at a point. -/
theorem charModule_smul_apply (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (a : A.A)
    (l : CharacterModule M.M) (x : M.M) : (a • l) x = l (MulOpposite.op a • x) := rfl

/-- The left `A`-action on characters extends the `R`-action. -/
theorem charIsScalarTower (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) :
    IsScalarTower R A.A (CharacterModule M.M) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul (fun r l => by
    ext x
    rw [charModule_smul_apply]
    rw [show MulOpposite.op (algebraMap R A.A r) = algebraMap R A.Aᵐᵒᵖ r from rfl,
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul]
    rfl)

attribute [local instance] charIsScalarTower

/-! ### The graded pieces of the dual -/

/-- The degree-`n` part of the graded dual: the characters of `M` supported on `M^{-n}`. -/
def dualPiece (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (n : ℤ) : Submodule R (CharacterModule M.M) where
  carrier := {l | ∀ m : ℤ, m ≠ -n → ∀ x ∈ M.grading m, l x = 0}
  zero_mem' := by intro m _ x _; rfl
  add_mem' := by
    intro l l' hl hl' m hm x hx
    rw [show ((l + l') x) = l x + l' x from rfl, hl m hm x hx, hl' m hm x hx, add_zero]
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r l hl m hm x hx
    rw [CharacterModule.smul_apply]
    exact hl m hm (r • x) ((M.grading m).smul_mem r hx)

/-- Unfolding of membership in `dualPiece`. -/
theorem mem_dualPiece {M : DifferentialGradedModule A} {n : ℤ} {l : CharacterModule M.M} :
    l ∈ dualPiece M n ↔ ∀ m : ℤ, m ≠ -n → ∀ x ∈ M.grading m, l x = 0 := Iff.rfl

/-- A character lying in the supremum of the graded pieces of degree `≠ n` kills `M^{-n}`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_mem_iSup_ne_dualPiece {M : DifferentialGradedModule A} {n : ℤ}
    {l : CharacterModule M.M} (hl : l ∈ ⨆ m, ⨆ (_ : m ≠ n), dualPiece M m)
    {x : M.M} (hx : x ∈ M.grading (-n)) : l x = 0 := by
  induction hl using Submodule.iSup_induction' with
  | mem m z hz =>
      by_cases hmn : m = n
      · rw [hmn] at hz
        simp only [ne_eq, not_true_eq_false, iSup_false, Submodule.mem_bot] at hz
        rw [hz]; rfl
      · rw [iSup_pos hmn] at hz
        exact hz (-n) (fun h => hmn (by omega)) x hx
  | zero => rfl
  | add y z _ _ ihy ihz => rw [show ((y + z) x) = y x + z x from rfl, ihy, ihz, add_zero]

/-- The graded pieces of the dual are independent. -/
theorem dualPiece_iSupIndep (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : iSupIndep (dualPiece M) := by
  rw [iSupIndep_def]
  intro n
  rw [Submodule.disjoint_def]
  intro l hl hl'
  ext x
  refine induction_homogeneous (M := M) (p := fun y => l y = 0) x (fun m y hy => ?_)
    (map_zero l) (fun y z hy hz => by rw [map_add l y z, hy, hz, add_zero])
  by_cases hm : m = -n
  · exact eq_zero_of_mem_iSup_ne_dualPiece hl' (hm ▸ hy)
  · exact hl m hm y hy

/-- The carrier of the graded dual, as an `R`-submodule: the characters that are sums of
homogeneous ones. -/
def dualCarrier (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : Submodule R (CharacterModule M.M) :=
  ⨆ n, dualPiece M n

/-- Unfolding of membership in `dualCarrier`. -/
theorem mem_dualCarrier {M : DifferentialGradedModule A} {l : CharacterModule M.M} :
    l ∈ dualCarrier M ↔ l ∈ ⨆ n, dualPiece M n := Iff.rfl

/-- The left action of a homogeneous element shifts the degree of a homogeneous character. -/
theorem charSMul_mem_dualPiece (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) {n m : ℤ}
    {l : CharacterModule M.M} (hl : l ∈ dualPiece M n) {a : A.A} (ha : a ∈ A.grading m) :
    charSMul M a l ∈ dualPiece M (n + m) := by
  intro j hj x hx
  rw [charSMul_apply]
  exact hl (j + m) (by omega) _ (M.smul_mem j m x a hx ha)

/-- An additive map on characters shifting the degree of homogeneous characters by `k` preserves
the carrier of the graded dual. -/
private theorem mem_dualCarrier_of_shift (M : DifferentialGradedModule A)
    (f : CharacterModule M.M →+ CharacterModule M.M) (k : ℤ)
    (hf : ∀ (n : ℤ) (l : CharacterModule M.M), l ∈ dualPiece M n → f l ∈ dualPiece M (n + k))
    {l : CharacterModule M.M} (hl : l ∈ dualCarrier M) : f l ∈ dualCarrier M := by
  rw [mem_dualCarrier] at hl ⊢
  induction hl using Submodule.iSup_induction' with
  | mem n z hz => exact Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (n + k) (hf n z hz)
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add z z' _ _ ihz ihz' => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ihz ihz'

/-- The left action by a homogeneous element preserves the carrier of the graded dual. -/
theorem charSMul_mem_dualCarrier_of_mem (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) {m : ℤ} {a : A.A}
    (ha : a ∈ A.grading m) {l : CharacterModule M.M} (hl : l ∈ dualCarrier M) :
    charSMul M a l ∈ dualCarrier M :=
  mem_dualCarrier_of_shift M (AddMonoidHom.mk' (charSMul M a) fun _ _ => by ext x; rfl) m
    (fun _ _ hz => charSMul_mem_dualPiece M hz ha) hl

/-- Left action by an algebra element, as an additive map in the algebra element. -/
def charSMulHom (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (l : CharacterModule M.M) :
    A.A →+ CharacterModule M.M :=
  AddMonoidHom.mk' (fun a => charSMul M a l) (fun a b => by
    ext x
    rw [charSMul_apply]
    simp only [MulOpposite.op_add, add_smul]
    rw [map_add]
    rfl)

/-- `charSMulHom M l` sends `a` to `charSMul M a l`. -/
@[simp] theorem charSMulHom_apply (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (l : CharacterModule M.M)
    (a : A.A) : charSMulHom M l a = charSMul M a l := rfl

/-- The left action by an arbitrary algebra element preserves the carrier of the graded dual. -/
theorem charSMul_mem_dualCarrier (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (a : A.A)
    {l : CharacterModule M.M} (hl : l ∈ dualCarrier M) : charSMul M a l ∈ dualCarrier M := by
  classical
  have hsum : ∑ m ∈ DFinsupp.support (DirectSum.decompose A.grading a),
      ((DirectSum.decompose A.grading a) m : A.A) = a :=
    DirectSum.sum_support_decompose A.grading a
  have key : charSMul M a l
      = ∑ m ∈ DFinsupp.support (DirectSum.decompose A.grading a),
          charSMul M ((DirectSum.decompose A.grading a) m : A.A) l := by
    have h0 : charSMul M a l = charSMulHom M l a := rfl
    rw [h0]
    conv_lhs => rw [← hsum]
    rw [map_sum]
    rfl
  rw [key]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ (fun m _ =>
    charSMul_mem_dualCarrier_of_mem M ((DirectSum.decompose A.grading a) m).2 hl)

/-- The carrier of the graded dual, as a left `A`-submodule of the character module. -/
def dualSub (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : Submodule A.A (CharacterModule M.M) where
  carrier := {l | l ∈ dualCarrier M}
  zero_mem' := (dualCarrier M).zero_mem
  add_mem' ha hb := (dualCarrier M).add_mem ha hb
  smul_mem' a _ hl := charSMul_mem_dualCarrier M a hl

/-- Restricting `dualSub` to `R` recovers `dualCarrier`. -/
theorem dualSub_restrictScalars (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) :
    (dualSub M).restrictScalars R = dualCarrier M := by
  apply SetLike.coe_injective; rfl

/-! ### The dual differential -/

/-- The differential of the graded dual: precomposition with `signedDifferential`. -/
def dualD0 (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) :
    CharacterModule M.M →ₗ[R] CharacterModule M.M :=
  CharacterModule.dual (signedDifferential M)

/-- The dual differential, evaluated at a point. -/
@[simp] theorem dualD0_apply (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (l : CharacterModule M.M)
    (x : M.M) : dualD0 M l x = l (signedDifferential M x) := rfl

/-- The dual differential raises the degree of a homogeneous character by one. -/
theorem dualD0_mem_dualPiece (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) {n : ℤ}
    {l : CharacterModule M.M} (hl : l ∈ dualPiece M n) :
    dualD0 M l ∈ dualPiece M (n + 1) := by
  intro j hj x hx
  rw [dualD0_apply, signedDifferential_apply_mem M hx, map_neg, map_zsmul,
    hl (j + 1) (by omega) _ (M.d_mem j x hx), smul_zero, neg_zero]

/-- The dual differential preserves the carrier of the graded dual. -/
theorem dualD0_mem_dualCarrier (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) {l : CharacterModule M.M}
    (hl : l ∈ dualCarrier M) : dualD0 M l ∈ dualCarrier M :=
  mem_dualCarrier_of_shift M (dualD0 M).toAddMonoidHom 1
    (fun _ _ hz => dualD0_mem_dualPiece M hz) hl

/-- The dual differential is square-zero. -/
theorem dualD0_comp_dualD0 (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) :
    (dualD0 M).comp (dualD0 M) = 0 := by
  rw [dualD0, ← CharacterModule.dual_comp, signedDifferential_comp_self,
    CharacterModule.dual_zero]

/-- The sign identity `(-1)^m (-1)^{j+m} = (-1)^j`. -/
theorem negOnePow_split (j m : ℤ) :
    (m.negOnePow : ℤ) * ((j + m).negOnePow : ℤ) = (j.negOnePow : ℤ) := by
  have h : m.negOnePow * (j + m).negOnePow = j.negOnePow := by
    rw [Int.negOnePow_add,
      show m.negOnePow * (j.negOnePow * m.negOnePow)
        = j.negOnePow * (m.negOnePow * m.negOnePow) by ac_rfl,
      Int.units_mul_self, mul_one]
  exact_mod_cast congrArg Units.val h

/-- The sign identity `(-1)^j (-1)^j = 1`. -/
theorem negOnePow_mul_self (j : ℤ) : (j.negOnePow : ℤ) * (j.negOnePow : ℤ) = 1 := by
  rw [← Units.val_mul, Int.units_mul_self, Units.val_one]

/-- The integer scalar action on characters, evaluated at a point. -/
theorem zsmul_char_apply (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) (c : ℤ)
    (ch : CharacterModule M.M) (y : M.M) : (c • ch) y = c • ch y := rfl

/-- The Leibniz rule for the graded dual, at the level of characters: for `a ∈ A^m`,
`d (a · λ) = (d a) · λ + (-1)^m (a · d λ)`, for an arbitrary character `λ`. -/
theorem dualD0_charSMul (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) {m : ℤ}
    (l : CharacterModule M.M) {a : A.A} (ha : a ∈ A.grading m) :
    dualD0 M (charSMul M a l)
      = charSMul M (A.d a) l + (m.negOnePow : ℤ) • charSMul M a (dualD0 M l) := by
  ext y
  refine induction_homogeneous (M := M) (p := fun z =>
    dualD0 M (charSMul M a l) z
      = (charSMul M (A.d a) l + (m.negOnePow : ℤ) • charSMul M a (dualD0 M l)) z)
    y (fun j z hz => ?_) (by simp) (fun z z' hz hz' => by rw [map_add, map_add, hz, hz'])
  have hL : dualD0 M (charSMul M a l) z
      = -((j.negOnePow : ℤ) • l (MulOpposite.op a • M.d z)) := by
    rw [dualD0_apply, signedDifferential_apply_mem M hz, map_neg, map_zsmul]
    rfl
  have hR : (charSMul M (A.d a) l + (m.negOnePow : ℤ) • charSMul M a (dualD0 M l)) z
      = l (MulOpposite.op (A.d a) • z)
        + -((j.negOnePow : ℤ) • l (MulOpposite.op a • M.d z)
            + l (MulOpposite.op (A.d a) • z)) := by
    change charSMul M (A.d a) l z + ((m.negOnePow : ℤ) • charSMul M a (dualD0 M l)) z = _
    rw [zsmul_char_apply]
    simp only [charSMul_apply, dualD0_apply]
    rw [signedDifferential_apply_mem M (M.smul_mem j m z a hz ha),
      M.leibniz j m z a hz ha, map_neg, map_zsmul, map_add, map_zsmul, smul_neg, smul_smul,
      negOnePow_split, smul_add, smul_smul, negOnePow_mul_self, one_smul]
  rw [hL, hR]
  abel

end DifferentialGradedModule.CharacterDual

namespace DifferentialGradedModule

open CharacterDual

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {A : DifferentialGradedAlgebra R}

attribute [local instance] CharacterDual.charModule CharacterDual.charIsScalarTower

/-- The graded `ℚ/ℤ`-dual `M^∨` of a right differential graded `A`-module, a *left*
differential graded `A`-module. -/
def dual (M : DifferentialGradedModule A) : DifferentialGraded.LeftModule A where
  M := ↥(dualSub M)
  isScalarTower := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul (fun r x => Subtype.ext
    (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul A.A r (x : CharacterModule M.M)))
  grading := Submodule.inducedGrading (dualPiece M) ((dualSub M).restrictScalars R)
  decomposition := Submodule.inducedGrading.decompositionOfEqISup (dualPiece M)
    (dualPiece_iSupIndep M) ((dualSub M).restrictScalars R) (dualSub_restrictScalars M)
  smul_mem := by
    intro m n a x ha hx
    refine Submodule.mem_inducedGrading.mpr ?_
    have h := charSMul_mem_dualPiece M (Submodule.mem_inducedGrading.mp hx) ha
    rwa [add_comm n m] at h
  d := LinearMap.restrict (dualD0 M) (p := (dualSub M).restrictScalars R)
    (q := (dualSub M).restrictScalars R) (fun x hx => dualD0_mem_dualCarrier M hx)
  d_comp_d := LinearMap.ext (fun x => Subtype.ext
    (LinearMap.congr_fun (dualD0_comp_dualD0 M) (x : CharacterModule M.M)))
  d_mem := by
    intro n x hx
    exact Submodule.mem_inducedGrading.mpr
      (dualD0_mem_dualPiece M (Submodule.mem_inducedGrading.mp hx))
  leibniz := by
    intro m n a x ha _hx
    exact Subtype.ext (dualD0_charSMul M (x : CharacterModule M.M) ha)

/-- The graded dual of the regular right module is `A^∨` as a left module. -/
def dualRegular (A : DifferentialGradedAlgebra R) : DifferentialGraded.LeftModule A :=
  dual (regularModule A)

end DifferentialGradedModule

end
